	* ROOT Macro (`macros/MeanAnnualTempLund.C`): 
	  - New ROOT macro. 
	  - Calculates annual mean temperatures
	  - Integrated a 30-year moving average graph (`TGraph`) and multi-period 
	    linear trend fits (`TF1`).
	  - Polished figure visualization by refining the y-axis range (4.5 to 12.5) 
	    and positioning a custom `TLegend` in the top-right corner to ensure a 
	    clean, report-ready presentation and saved in the figures folder.

2026-11-9 Ewucok

	*Added
	 - Data Completeness Threshold: Implemented a filtering criterion (minDays = 330) in   		MeanAnnualTempLundClean.C to remove years with incomplete seasonal coverage (specifically excluding sparse years like 1957–1960).
	 - Decadal Slope Reporting: Added stdout logging to compute and print temperature warming rates per decade for all three fit periods directly from TF1 fit parameters.
	 - Excluded Year Auditing: Added console listing for skipped years failing the threshold check.
	 
	*Changed
	 - Data Representation: Transitioned from a histogram (TH1D) to a TGraph (ALP draw mode) for annual mean temperatures. This eliminates zero/sentinel dips in the time series when years are missing.
	 - Fit Boundary Calibration: Adjusted the upper boundary of the modern linear fit (f3) from 2022 to 2007 to align with the termination point of the 30-year moving average window (2022 - 15).
	 - Legend & Plot Styling: Updated the legend to explicitly list individual fit intervals (1795-1850, 1850-1970, 1970-2007) alongside the moving average and daily scatter/line points. Set vertical axis boundaries to (4.5, 12.5) for consistent visual comparison